# Golden test fixtures are byte-significant: test code compares them with
# string(want) != got (see update_golden_test.go, sse golden test). With
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows, git would convert LF<->CRLF on checkout and
# break those byte-exact comparisons. Mark these -text (no EOL conversion) so
# the checked-out bytes always equal the committed canonical bytes.
internal/cli/tui/testdata/*.txt -text
internal/proto/testdata/*.txt -text
